#: src/libvlc-module.c:253
msgid "Drift readings needed before correcting audibly"
msgstr ""

#: src/libvlc-module.c:255
msgid ""
"Flushing the audio output or padding it with silence is audible, and a "
"single late measurement -- one scheduling hiccup -- used to be enough to "
"trigger it. Require this many consecutive measurements instead. Set to 1 for "
"the historical behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: src/libvlc-module.c:261
msgid "Correct audio drift by inserting silence"
msgstr ""

#: src/libvlc-module.c:263
msgid ""
"When the audio output has drifted ahead of the input clock, it can be padded "
"with silence to realign. That keeps audio in step with video, at the cost of "
"an audible gap; letting the resampler absorb the offset instead is inaudible "
"but slow, and leaves audio slightly ahead until it catches up. By default "
"this is decided per stream: padding is used only when there is video or a "
"stream output to stay in step with."
msgstr ""

